 index←{x}Select choices;flag;answer;question;value;bool;⎕ML;⎕IO;manyFlag;mustFlag;caption;buff;flag2;alias;spaceFlag;firstPart;Select_Choices;keyword;newIndex;rangeFlag;minSel;maxSel;allFlag;quitFlag;helpFlag
⍝ Presents `choices` as a numbered list & allows the user to select exactly one or multiple ones or none.
⍝ Selecting exactly one or none is the default.\\
⍝ `choices` must be a vector of character vectors; leading spaces in them are removed.\\
⍝ The optional left argument allows you to specify multiple (positional) choices:
⍝  * `caption` is shown above the choices; must be a simple character vector
⍝  * `manyFlag` defaults to 0 (= just 1 item might be selected) or 1 (allow selecting multiple items).
⍝    Rather than a Boolean it may also be two integers `(min max)`: the user must then select at least
⍝    `min` and at most `max` items, so `(2 2)` means "exactly two". Both must be integers between 1 and
⍝    the number of choices, and `min` must not be greater than `max`.
⍝  * `mustFlag` forces the user to select at least one item: pressing `<enter>` without a selection is rejected
⍝  * `quitFlag` decides whether the user may enter "q" (for "quit"), which returns ¯1. It defaults to
⍝    `~mustFlag`, so pass a 1 together with `mustFlag←1` in order to enforce a selection but still allow
⍝    the user to quit\\
⍝ Returns a scalar in case a single item was selected, a vector in case more than one item was
⍝ selected, `⍬` in case the user did not enter anything and ¯1 if the user entered "q" for "quit".\\
⍝ Notes:
⍝  * `choices` must not have more than 999 items\\
⍝  * Duplicates entered by the user are removed before the number of selected items is checked\\
⍝  * With `manyFlag←1` the user may also enter an "a" for "all", or `a~{n}` for "all but n", with n
⍝    being one or more item numbers. Under `mustFlag` `a~{n}` must not exclude every single item.
⍝    With `manyFlag←(min max)` these two keywords are not on offer.\\
⍝  * When more than one item may be selected, the user may also enter ranges like `3-6` for `3 4 5 6`,
⍝    mixed with single numbers as in `1 2 5 10-13 17`; commas are treated like spaces. A range must not
⍝    contain spaces, and its second number must be greater than the first one. Ranges may also follow
⍝    `a~`, as in `a~10-40`. In automation a value like `'3-6'` is matched against the choices, though.\\
⍝  * The prompt does not list any of this syntax; it offers `(Get help with ?)` instead. Entering a `?` puts
⍝    the choices on display again with the help injected just above the input line, see `SelectHelp`\\
⍝  * `mustFlag` and `quitFlag` keep their meaning with `(min max)`\\
⍝  * By entering "`∘∘∘`" the user may interrupt `Select` by running onto a stop vector, overcoming
⍝    the Dyalog bug that ⍞ cannot be interrupted
⍝  * You can automate `Select`, refer to the documentation with ]ADoc CommTools, catchword "Automation".
⍝    Note that automation is restricted by none of `manyFlag`, `(min max)` and `quitFlag`
 ⎕IO←1 ⋄ ⎕ML←1
 x←{0<⎕NC ⍵:⊆⍎⍵ ⋄ ''}'x'
 (caption manyFlag mustFlag quitFlag)←x,(≢x)↓'' 0 0 ⍬
 quitFlag←mustFlag{⍬≡⍵:~⍺ ⋄ ⍵}quitFlag
 '"quitFlag" must be a Boolean'Assert(⊂quitFlag)∊0 1
 '"caption" must be a simple character vector'Assert 1=≡caption←,caption
 '"caption" must not contain line feeds (⎕UCS 10)'Assert~LF∊caption
 '"caption" must not contain carriage returns (⎕UCS 13)'Assert~(⎕UCS 13)∊caption
 'Invalid right argument; must be a vector of text vectors.'⎕SIGNAL ErrNo/⍨2≠|≡choices
 'Right argument has more than 999 items'⎕SIGNAL ErrNo/⍨999<≢choices
 :If rangeFlag←1<≢manyFlag
     '"min" and "max" must be integers between 1 and the number of choices'Assert∧/manyFlag∊⍳≢choices
     (minSel maxSel)←manyFlag
     '"min" must not be greater than "max"'Assert minSel≤maxSel
     allFlag←0
 :Else
     '"manyFlag" must be a Boolean or two integers (min max)'Assert(⊃,manyFlag)∊0 1
     allFlag←⊃,manyFlag
     minSel←1
     maxSel←(1+allFlag)⊃1(≢choices)
 :EndIf
 flag←0
 firstPart←{⍵↑⍨⍵⍳LF}caption
 :If 0<⎕NC'∆Automation'
 :AndIf 0<≢∆Automation
     Select_Choices←(∆Automation[;1]≡¨⊂'Select')⌿∆Automation[;2 3]
 :AndIf 0<≢Select_Choices
     :If AliasChar∊caption
         (alias caption)←SplitAlias caption
         flag←0<+/bool←(TakeAlias¨Select_Choices[;1])≡¨⊂alias
     :Else
         flag←0<+/bool←caption∘≡¨Select_Choices[;1]
     :EndIf
     :If flag
         'Multiple choices qualify?!'Assert 1=+/bool
         index←2⊃Select_Choices[bool⍳1;]
         'Select'Log⊃Select_Choices[bool⍳1;]
         :If (⊂index)∊0 ⍬
             index←⍬
         :ElseIf ' '=1↑0⍴∊index ⍝ Text?!
             (keyword newIndex)←choices ParseSelectKeyword index
             :If '*'=¯1↑index
                 index←⍸((¯1+≢index)↑¨DropLeadingSpaces¨choices)≡¨⊂¯1↓index
                 'Invalid selection'Assert(mustFlag{(0<≢⍵)≠⍺}index)∨∨/index∊⍳≢choices
             :ElseIf '*'=⊃index
                 index←⍸((-¯1+≢index)↑¨DropTrailingSpaces¨choices)≡¨⊂1↓index
                 'Invalid selection'Assert(mustFlag{(0<≢⍵)≠⍺}index)∨∨/index∊⍳≢choices
             :ElseIf (,'q')≡,index
                 index←¯1
             :ElseIf 0<≢keyword
                 index←newIndex
                 :If 'a~'≡keyword
                     'Invalid selection'Assert mustFlag≤0<≢index ⍝ Must not exclude every item
                 :EndIf
             :ElseIf 0<≢buff←⍸index∘≡¨choices
                 index←buff
                 'Invalid selection'Assert index∊⍳≢choices
             :ElseIf 1=≢index←⍸index∘≡¨(≢index)↑¨DropLeadingSpaces¨choices
                 index←⊃index
                 'Invalid selection'Assert index∊⍳≢choices
             :Else
                 'Invalid selection'Assert 0
             :EndIf
         :Else
             'Invalid selection'Assert∧/index∊⍳≢choices
             index←∪index ⍝ The caller might have specified an item twice
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
 :If ~flag
     flag2←0
     helpFlag←0
     :If rangeFlag
         :If minSel=maxSel
             question←'Select exactly ',(⍕minSel),' item',(1<minSel)/'s'
         :Else
             question←'Select ',(⍕minSel),' to ',(⍕maxSel),' items'
         :EndIf
     :Else
         question←'Select one ',(allFlag/'or more '),'item',allFlag/'s'
     :EndIf
     question,←' (Get help with ?) :'
     spaceFlag←0≠≢caption
     :If AliasChar∊caption
         :If (firstPart⍳' ')>firstPart⍳AliasChar
             caption←DropAlias caption
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
     'Select'CallOnWait caption
     :Repeat
         ⍞←({⍵↑'---',(spaceFlag/' '),caption,(spaceFlag/' '),⍵⍴'-'}⎕PW-2),LF
         ⍞←⍕↑{((⊂'. '),¨⍨(⊂3 0)⍕¨⍳≢⍵),¨⍵}choices
         ⍞←2⍴LF
         :If helpFlag
             ⍞←↑SelectHelp mustFlag quitFlag allFlag maxSel
             ⍞←LF
             helpFlag←0
         :EndIf
         :If 0<≢answer←⍞,0/⍞←question
             answer←{⍵↑⍨-¯1+(⌽⍵)⍳':'}answer
             :If '∘∘∘'≡¯3↑answer
                 (1+⊃⎕LC)⎕STOP⊃⎕SI
                 ∘∘∘ ⍝ Deliberate stop caused by user input
             :EndIf
             :If (,'?')≡,answer
                 helpFlag←1
                 :Continue ⍝ Put the help on display and ask again
             :EndIf
             (keyword newIndex)←choices ParseSelectKeyword ⎕C answer
             :If (,'q')≡keyword
                 :If quitFlag
                     index←¯1
                     flag2←1
                 :EndIf
             :ElseIf (,'a')≡keyword
                 :If allFlag
                     index←newIndex
                     flag2←1
                 :EndIf
             :ElseIf 'a~'≡keyword
                 :If allFlag
                     index←newIndex
                     flag2←0≠≢index ⍝ Must not exclude every item
                 :EndIf
             :Else
                 :If (0=≢answer)∧~mustFlag
                     index←⍬ ⋄ →0
                 :EndIf
                 (bool value)←(≢choices)ParseSelectNumbers answer
                 :If bool
                     value←∪value ⍝ The user might have entered an item twice
                     :If ∧/value∊⍳≢choices
                     :AndIf minSel≤≢value
                     :AndIf maxSel≥≢value
                         index←value
                         flag2←1
                     :EndIf
                 :EndIf
             :EndIf
         :EndIf
     :Until flag2
 :EndIf
 index←{1<≢⍵:⍵ ⋄ ⊃⍵}⍣(⍬≢index)⊣index
⍝Done
